+# Historical Archive Sources Guide
+
+Find primary sources, newspaper archives, and historical records.
+
+---
+
+## Digital Archive Collections
+
+### Internet Archive
+**URL**: https://archive.org/
+
+**Collections**:
+- **Wayback Machine**: Historical website snapshots
+- **Books**: Millions of digitized books
+- **Newspapers**: Historical newspaper scans
+- **Audio/Video**: Historical recordings
+
+**Search tips**:
+- Use collection filters
+- Date range searches
+- Full-text search in books
+
+### Library of Congress
+**URL**: https://www.loc.gov/
+
+**Key Collections**:
+- **Chronicling America**: Historic newspapers (1770s-1960s)
+  https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/
+- **American Memory**: Primary source collections
+- **Prints & Photographs**: Historical images
+
+### Google Books
+**URL**: https://books.google.com/
+
+- Preview mode for copyrighted works
+- Full text for public domain
+- Good for finding specific passages
+
+---
+
+## Newspaper Archives
+
+### Free Resources
+
+**Chronicling America** (LOC)
+- https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/
+- US newspapers 1770s-1960s
+- Full-text searchable
+
+**Google News Archive**
+- https://news.google.com/newspapers
+- Limited but free
+- Good for 20th century
+
+**Elephind**
+- https://elephind.com/
+- Aggregates free newspaper archives
+- International coverage
+
+### Paid Resources
+
+**Newspapers.com**
+- Most comprehensive US coverage
+- 1700s-present
+- Subscription or library access
+
+**ProQuest Historical Newspapers**
+- Major papers (NYT, WSJ, etc.)
+- Library access typically required
+
+**NewspaperArchive.com**
+- International coverage
+- Subscription required
+
+---
+
+## Government Historical Records
+
+### National Archives (NARA)
+**URL**: https://www.archives.gov/
+
+**Key resources**:
+- Federal records
+- Military records
+- Census data
+- Historical photographs
+
+### FBI Vault
+**URL**: https://vault.fbi.gov/
+
+- Declassified FBI files
+- Famous cases and investigations
+- FOIA releases
+
+### CIA Reading Room
+**URL**: https://www.cia.gov/readingroom/
+
+- Declassified intelligence
+- Historical operations
+- Cold War documents
+
+### Government Publishing Office
+**URL**: https://www.govinfo.gov/
+
+- Congressional records
+- Federal Register
+- Historical government publications
+
+---
+
+## Finding Contemporary Coverage
+
+### Why Contemporary Sources Matter
+- Written before outcome known
+- Captures uncertainty of the moment
+- Different framing than retrospective
+- Language of the era
+
+### Search Strategies
+
+**By date range**:
+```
+"[event]" newspaper [month] [year]
+"[event]" site:newspapers.com
+"[event]" site:chroniclingamerica.loc.gov
+```
+
+**For specific publications**:
+```
+"[event]" site:nytimes.com before:1950
+"[event]" "New York Times" [year]
+```
+
+### Reading Historical News
+- Note sensationalism of era
+- Watch for bias (political, regional)
+- Cross-reference multiple papers
+- Check for corrections/follow-ups
+
+---
+
+## Academic and Research Archives
+
+### JSTOR
+**URL**: https://www.jstor.org/
+
+- Academic articles and books
+- Historical analysis
+- Many items free after registration
+
+### HathiTrust
+**URL**: https://www.hathitrust.org/
+
+- Digital library consortium
+- Millions of digitized books
+- Full text for public domain
+
+### University Digital Collections
+Many universities have specialized collections:
+- Regional history
+- Industry-specific archives
+- Personal papers
+- Photographs
+
+Search: `"[topic]" digital collection site:edu`
+
+---
+
+## Oral History Resources
+
+### StoryCorps
+**URL**: https://storycorps.org/
+
+- Personal narratives
+- Searchable archive
+- American experience focus
+
+### Library of Congress Oral Histories
+- Veterans History Project
+- Civil Rights History Project
+- Occupational Folklife Project
+
+### University Collections
+Search: `"[topic]" oral history site:edu`
+
+---
+
+## Working with Historical Documents
+
+### Source Evaluation
+- **Provenance**: Where did this come from?
+- **Authenticity**: Is it what it claims to be?
+- **Perspective**: Who created it, why?
+- **Corroboration**: Do other sources confirm?
+
+### Dating Documents
+- Publication date vs. event date
+- Consider when author wrote (perspective)
+- Note if retrospective account
+
+### Citing Historical Sources
+```markdown
+**Source**: [Archive name]
+**Title**: "[Document title]"
+**Date**: [Original date]
+**Collection**: [Collection name]
+**URL/Location**: [How to find it]
+**Accessed**: [When you accessed]
+```
+
+---
+
+## Era-Specific Tips
+
+| Era | Primary Sources | Challenges |
+|-----|-----------------|------------|
+| Pre-1860 | Letters, official records | Limited survival |
+| 1860-1920 | Newspapers, photographs | Bias, sensationalism |
+| 1920-1950 | Radio, newsreels, print | Audio/video rare |
+| 1950-1990 | TV, magazines, gov docs | Copyright restrictions |
+| 1990-2010 | Early web, digitized print | Dead links, format issues |
+
+---
+
+## For Lyrics
+
+### Period Language
+Research the language of the era:
+- Newspaper headlines
+- Contemporary speeches
+- Slang dictionaries
+- Period fiction
+
+### Authentic Details
+- Exact dates from contemporary sources
+- Names/titles as used at the time
+- Dollar amounts (note inflation)
+- Place names (may have changed)
